\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 Honouring Dishonour
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \
Shielding Richard from the glare of the formidable security and surveillance capacity of the Primary Trade Dominion was going to be next to impossible. To take the Commissioner\'92s chair Hayley had to deliver unto the CEO a bona fide Elvi Saviour and she could not just substitute some random child in the place of Richard. Apart from the stomach churning amorality, she knew would not get it past the CEO. He was just too shrewed. 
\f3\i Does it have to be a child\cf2 ? \cf0 She thought vacantly. She then thought to contact the High Elvis. 
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 - - -
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \'93Thank you, your Elvisness.\'94 Agent Jones said, so happy his contribution had been noticed. \'93This is the greatest honour of my life.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Nothing you do not deserve, Agent Jones. I assure you.\'94 The High Elvis said, grim. \'93Let\'92s take our places.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 Every member of the Elvi Parliament was present in the chamber, splendid in ornate official parliamentary red and gold regalia, silent and dignified. The public gallery was packed with chattering Elvises and Elvines, cheerfully waiting for the pageantry to begin. They were trusted the family members of the parliamentarians below, but still considered themselves lucky to being a part of history.
\f0 \

\f2 Agent Jones, draped in a floor length hooded cape of glimmering blue satin, entered the Chamber from the speaker\'92s side entrance to uproarious applause. Smiling and nodding, he slipped across the chamber slowly and deliberately, taking in the long sought after applause. Members of parliament and spectators alike were standing and cheering as he silently centred himself in the chamber.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Our saviour!\'94 An enthusiastic spectator called out. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Not our saviour!\'94 The High Elvis took the podium to silence. \'93He is \ul \ulc0 The\ulnone  Saviour!\'94 The chamber roared with approval. \'93Let me tell you what he has done for the Elvi nation. He was an assassin was sworn to uphold the security of the PTD, but he saw the righteousness of our cause and he pledged himself to us!\'94
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \'93Praise be unto him.\'94 Cried out the Minister of Defence, precisely as the script demanded. The parliament erupted into ecstatic applause taking quite a few minutes to die down.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Yes, praise be unto him.\'94 The High Elvis nearly choked on his words. \'93He went on a secret mission for us, to deliver a contagion and wiping out the threat from those who conspire against us.\'94 The crown hissed on cue. \'93He lead a team of agents on a suicide mission strike at the heart of their conspiracy. The bodies of those agents were left for us to see, but the mission was a success. With all of their viral agents destroyed we can look to the future with some confidence, thanks to you Agent Jones.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I thank you and my Elvi friends everywhere.\'94 Agent Jones bowed deeply, pausing reverently and with unbending back, gracefully raised himself upright. \'93I am pledged only to the Elvi.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I put a motion, the only motion tonight, to this very special sitting of parliament. I ask that the chamber to declare today and for all time that our friend Agent Jones be not only born to us a new member of the Elvi Nation, but born to us as the Saviour of the Elvi. Great Saviour\'94 H.E bowed.
\f0 \

\f2 The gallery went crazy, jumping up and down calling out \'93Great Saviour\'94 over and over, a few feinting with ecstasy, others sobbed and hugged. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I call upon parliament to vote on the motion.\'94 H.E. \'93Mr Speaker, you have the floor.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 Members in the chamber quietly recorded their votes in the recently installed voting system. Nothing too fancy, votes were generally a yes or no proposition, so all you had to do was press the red or the green button. The Speaker had the results in minutes and stood up before the awaiting mob.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93On the single proposition before us tonight, for the affirmative 99, for the negative 1. The motion is passed. Agent Jones is born to us new member of the Elvi Nation and declared The Great Saviour!\'94 The speaker managed to get out most of it before being drowned out by the crowd. 
\f3\i Who the fuck voted against the motion?
\f0\i0 \

\f2 \'93Come forward Great Saviour\'94 H.E. motioned Agent Jones before him. \'93Bow your head. I hereby crown you Great Saviour of the Elvi.\'94 H.E. wanted to place a grass crown upon Agent Jones\'92 head, but since only the ultra rich had the coin to maintain a lawn, they made do with an intricately woven, thorny vine.
\f0 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 - - -
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \'93Sarah?\'94 Hayley asked over the encrypted channel. \'93I think they are about to move. Are you secure?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Not at this point in time. I will see what I can arrange.\'94 Sarah replied. \'93This is it isn\'92t it?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Good luck, Holy Mother.\'94 Hayley\'92s anxiety hung in the air before she cut call. From the few fragments of intel she had scraped together, it seemed Haloren Smythe had identified Richard and was closing in. The CEO had approved unlimited resources and he had syphoned units from everywhere including, most recently, her surveillance and tactical teams. She sent all the gung-ho, jarheads she could gather in the they would fuck it up. 
\f3\i Good luck keeping those boys under control Mr Smythe.
\f0\i0 \

\f2 Surveillance operatives had followed Sarah, Richard and the Elvi Security team to a very exclusive part of the city. Although the Elvi had set up multiple decoy operations, they felt it was more probable that not, they were now following the right baby-saviour. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Sir, they are at 12896 Goldstream. High Security, but we have tanks and are confident of a fast entry.\'94 Radioed in the lead surveillance operative to his boss Haloren Smythe. Are you sure we have got the right kid? They all look the fucken same to me.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We cannot be 100% certain, but I don\'92t have the luxury of time.\'94 Haloren wanted to win this competition quickly and all of the intelligence pointed to this kid. Even his name was a bit obvious, but he was not certain. 
\f3\i Fuck, this operational management thing is harder than I thought. 
\f2\i0 \'93Tell the entry team it\'92s a green light. Hard entry, extreme prejudice.\'94 No use having witnesses. 
\f3\i 12896 Goldstream? 
\f2\i0 The address seemed familiar.
\f0 \

\f2 The target premises was a massive and very rare free-standing dwelling, set on on entire acre of manicured lawn and surrounded by a 5 metre high security barrier of concrete and steel, virtually impenetrable and most likely electrified. The gate was was the obvious point of entry and the first attempt was made using a small tank that just ploughed in a top speed. The dent in the gate was minimal, but such was the impact the crew were rendered unconscious, having to be dragged out and replaced before another attempt could be made. So much for a quick entry.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What the fuck is that gate made from ?\'94 The leader of the entry team inquired loudly. Shoot the fucken thing off!\'94
\f0 \

\f2 The tank was reversed away from the gate and then it let out a massive plasma blast from the fat, stubby barrel poking out of the turret. The gate blew off it\'92s hinges and spun wildly along the slender driveway, digging up chunks of bitumen and dirt before hacking massive furrows in the lawn, exposing dark, rich soil. 
\f0 \

\f2 Two small tanks and an APC entered the gate and raced toward the house, one tank took to the rear and the other the front. 20 operatives in black entered the gate and fanned out, waiting for the breach. 
\f0 \

\f2 Elvi Security begged to secure Richard in some hidden vault, but Eloise had assured them the house was a vault itself. Unconvinced, they readied to engage the intruders, taking up defensive positions throughout the sprawling mansion. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Your men don\'92t have to worry.\'94 Eloise Shakti calmly informed Sarah from the comfort of her sofa. A pale, fragile tea set took centre place before her on the coffee table, the pot\'92s spout steaming enticingly. \'93This will be all over soon. Tea dear?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What about the team of killers outside?\'94 Sarah was beside herself with thoughts of losing her son, but Richard was happily playing on the floor, completely aware of his situation.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We are perfectly safe.\'94 Eloise insisted. \'93I am Eliose Shakti and my house is fortress, built of thick tungsten reinforced poly-crete and ballistic glass. It has automated defence systems and a squadron of drones. You will be safe and my grandson will be safe.\'94 It had only taken one look at Richard for her to see that this kid was special and placing him in danger was unfathomable. \'94In the unlikely event that any of these people gain entry, we will need more than the pop-guns your security are carrying. She stood up, tea cup daintily in hand and traversed the room to an innocuous panel in the wall and placed her hand on a sensor pad. The panel clicked open to reveal a cache of serious firepower. \'93This is the Primary Trade Dominion.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93By the power of finance! I\'92ve have never seen weapons of this type.\'94 Sarah was a daughter of the PTD and could not help but be impressed by the state of art weaponry.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93There\'92s a cabinet like this in every room and I have unlocked them all.\'94 Eloise smiled. \'93These are advanced prototypes of pulse rifles and these are pulse cannons. Be careful of the PPP\'92s are extremely powerful. My companies manufacture them, of course.\'94 Eloise was a proud business woman. \'93There is a variety of smart-grenades - incendiary, electro-magnetic, sonic pulse and good old-fashioned fragment grenades.\'94 Mrs Shakti, the elder, was always prepared - in this case, perhaps, more than prepared.
\f0 \

\f2 The tanks kept their distance, waiting for the order to open fire as the APC slowly approached the massive portico at front of the house, mounting a set of six wide creamy-white onyx stairs, cracking the expensive masonry and crushing it to rubble. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93They cost a fortune!\'94 Eloise was incensed. Even for the ultra rich, stone of that quality was rare and she had only just had it installed. She opened the blinds of the huge front windows giving her a perfect view of the entry team and the response her defence systems were about to make. \'93Don\'92t worry dear, this will be over quickly.\'94 She took a sip of tea.
\f0 \

\f2 Sarah noted the the glass was impossibly thick, but did not seem to distort the light or the view. Upon seeing the police closing in, Sarah instinctively picked up Richard, cradling him close. She saw a solid square bollard, about one metre thick rise out of the grass, 3 metres in front of the APC and unleashed a blast from a pulse cannon, splitting it entirely up the centre. Through a wet pink mist, molten fragments of armour star burst in every direction. The shock wave knocked out anyone in a 30 metre radius, largely neutralising entry team at the front of the house. In response, the two tank commanders opened fire, striking the front and rear simultaneously, but did not seem to scratch the surface. Exterior Holo-emitters had kicked in, instantly covering the damage and deflating the egos of the tank commanders. Immediately, more bollards popped up and the tanks were instantly hit from all sides with a barrage of particle pulse fire. Elvis Security opened fire with PPP\'92s from inside the house, exploding black uniforms with their turbo charged pistols. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You were not kidding when you said it would be over quickly. How long did they last\cf2 ? \cf0 Two minutes?\'94 Sarah was in awe of her mother-in-law and was glad she was close-by when she she go the word from Hayley. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Mr Shakti and I always thought it would be a mob from the Pale that would try to over-run us, but the Police\cf2 ? \cf0 Get out there and mop up the rest...\'94 Eloise barked at the Elvi. They all stood in place until Sarah gave them a nod. \'93\'85but take one alive, I need to find out who sent them.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 The Elvis\'92 were merciless, blowing massive chunks out of anything in a black uniform, discriminating not between the unconscious and the upright. The lucky single prisoner was dragged before Eloise, Sarah and Richard, who was surrounded by a company of black haired guards. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You and your little band made a big mistake coming here. Did you not think I would be ready?\'94 Eloise was incensed. \'93Why did you come here here you stupid, stupid man?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93The child must die.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What? Why?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93He\'92s some sort of Messiah for the Elvi.\'94 He managed to squeak out before the lead security kicked him in the side. \'93He is a symbol of hope.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93A messiah? A symbol of hope\cf2 ? \cf0 He is my grandson and he will be afforded all of the protection my position provides.\'94 Grandma Shakti took a deep breath. \'93Now, who sent you?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We are on a CEO\'92s Directive to track down and neutralise the saviour of the Elvi. My commander is Haloren Smythe.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 Taking our her personal coms device, she called the CEO. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Eloise Shakti. Haloren Smythe ordered a raid on my house to murder my grandson, they think he is the Messiah \'85.. No, they are mostly dead \'85..You will have to pay for the clean-up\'85 They broke my set of Onyx stairs!\'85.Yes those ones! \'85\'85\'85\'85.Even if he is the Messiah, I don\'92t care. He is my grandson and my protection falls upon him. An attack upon him is an attack upon me. I hope you comprehend what I am saying. Goodbye.\'94 
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 - - -
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 The CEO was frozen in place, momentarily catatonic, wanting to go back a few minutes in time, back to the good old days when he had not pissed off Eloise Shakti. Coming back to the present he turned to Hayley Lanning, seated smugly on the other side of the desk.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93This vid evidence looks pretty solid. The ceremony in their parliament seems credible to me, but everything pointed towards a birth of a child. This is entirely unexpected.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You heard the High Elvis himself sir, Agent Jones was \'91born to the Elvi\'92 and they called him the great Saviour.\'94 Hayley decided to pile even on even more. \'93Look, I\'92ve identified the Elvis Messiah, I have identified who breached the security at your not-so-secret virus lab and I have ballistics that identify him for the murders of the family of a man named Emile Kalhari. A most brutal crime.\'94 
\f3\i I told you I would get you for that Agent Jones.
\f0\i0 \

\f2 \'93He is a rogue agent of the worst kind and he will be dealt with by The Directorate. They will interrogate and dispose of him.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93They won\'92t interrogate him. It will be murder pure and simple.\'94 Hayley feigned protest.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93It will be a sanctioned contract termination on my orders!\'94 The CEO was feeling a little better after that shock call from Eloise.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Yes, Sir.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You may leave, Commissioner Lanning.\'94 He gave her a wry smile. \'93The job is yours.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What about Haloren Smythe? What do I do with him?\'94 Immediately acting the Commissioner.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Nothing. He will be retiring shortly.\'94 He shuddered at the thought of what Grammy Shakti would do to the poor bastard. He will have no friends now and nowhere to hide. \'93He has done something very reckless. He tried to raid Eloise Shakti\'92s mansion.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93My goodness! How many casualties?\'94 
\f3\i She knew it wasn\'92t going to be pretty.
\f0\i0 \

\f2 \'9335 dead, 2 tanks and an ACP and two tanks destroyed.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Two tanks and and APC? They cost a fortune!\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93And they cracked her onyx stairs out the front, too.\'94 The CEO added, horrified.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93My goodness. Can you even get that anymore?\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I don\'92t know, but she said we are paying for the clean-up and by that I mean your department.\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Yes, sir.\'94 The damage bill notwithstanding, she was happy the Directorate would deal with Agent Jones. She did not want to try to effect an arrest of The Great Saviour, it would be most unbecoming for one of the Holy Aunts.
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 - - -
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 The next order of business was to drag Haloren Smythe into his office for a dressing down. The debacle would not and could not be forgiven. Within half an hour of being summonsed, Haloren Smythe, former candidate for Commissioner of Police, was standing on before him. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93How is the investigation progressing, Haloren?\'94 He was keen to hear the bullshit Haloren was about to spin.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Well sir, I have identified the child, but we had a set back. We mounted an arrest operation on an address on Goldstream, but we were repelled by automated defence systems.\'94 Haloren stuttered.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What intell did you have on the address itself?\'94 The CEO inquired.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93It was a fluid situation, sir and I had to act quickly. We had multiple decoy targets and had not identified all of the players, but we were certain we had zeroed in on the correct group of people.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93So you made a bold decision and went in.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93It seemed correct at the time.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Any losses?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Well,\'85yes. We lost an APC, two TT\'92s and 35 men.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Two tanks, you say?\'94 The CEO decided it was time to lower the boom. \'93You idiot! You imbecile! Raiding the home of Eloise Shakti, the PTD\'92s most prominent arms manufacturer, with zero intel. Do you know what you have done?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Eloise Shakti?\'94 Oh dear, w
\f3\i hat a monumental fuck up. \'93
\f2\i0 I was in the process of analysing our tactical alternative.\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Did you personally lay eyes on the property\cf2 ? \cf0 Any idiot could tell the house belonged to someone of substance.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Am I to try and extract the child again?\'94 Haloren figured he already knew the answer.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You will do nothing of the sort. You will stand down, immediately. Authorisation for resources is hereby rescinded. This farce is to end. Eloise Shankti has already been in my ear and she is as angry as she is rich.\'94 He paused for effect. \'94Do you really think the son of Alexander Shakti is the Saviour of the Elvi?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93If you say it like that it sounds a little absurd, but there is a timing anomaly with the pregnancy. Shakti may not be the father.\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Even if it is true, it does not matter. You have struck at the heart of the elite, your people. The same people who, when you were looking at a death sentence, plucked from your cell and set you free. The child is now protected by God herself and he is untouchable. In any case we have already identified the Saviour and he is not the son of Alexander Shakti.\'94 The CEO scoffed.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Impossible, my information is quite compelling. You have to listen, please.\'94 He knew he was finished.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Look at this video\'94 The CEO raised the holoscreen and the presentation began and they silently watched. \'93Quite compelling, isn\'92t it?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Where did you get it?\'94 Haloren asked, knowing it must be a ruse.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You under estimated the abilities of Commissioner Lanning, Mr Smythe. She managed to get hi-qual-vid of this naming ceremony for \'91The Great Saviour.\'92 It happened just last night. According to the High Elvis, can you believe the name? our very own Agent Jones, is now the most revered soul in the Elvi nation. They even gave him a crown.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93That\'92s absurd, the messiah is a newborn.\'94 Haloren said. 
\f3\i Commissioner Lanning?
\f0\i0 \

\f2 \'93Agent Jones was \'93born to the Elvi\'94 and named their Saviour because he lead a team of Elvi who raided one of my facilities, destroying decades of viral research.\'94 The CEO took a deep breath and suppressed a smile. 
\f3\i The Elvi think they have destroyed my killer virus! They think they are safe! A surprise awaits those pompous fools.
\f2\i0  \'93I am yet to alert the Directorate of Agent Jones\'92 treason and only because you are of executive stock I will give you a final opportunity to partially redeem yourself.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Anything, sir.\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I want you to terminate Agent Jones\'92 contract. Do you think you can manage that?\'94 The CEO liked to mock. \'93The books have to be tallied up by the end of business, tomorrow. You will then disappear, but you will not be free. Your friends will spurn you and your portfolio will wither. When I need you again I will contact.\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Thank you, I won\'92t let you down.\'94 Haloren Smythe. He felt like killing someone and slipping back into the underworld was something he looked forwards to.
\f0 \

\f2 The CEO sat contemplating his morning and his little scrape with Eloise. Her little grandson may not be related her at all. He tucked that little gem away for future reference. 
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 - - -
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 The new Commissioner was glad to leave to CEO\'92s office so quickly and with so few questions. She could not believe he had swallowed that \'91born again\'92 crap so easily and she also couldn\'92t believe her first act as Commissioner was to place a listening device in the CEO\'92s office. She still didn\'92t know the fate of Sarah and Richard and had an urgent call to make but she couldn\'92t call Sarah on her personal comms device and had make it back to her new office before she could make encrypted contact.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Oh Hayley, it was both terrifying and thrilling. Eloise says the defence system had hardly kicked into gear before wiping out the entry team. She was disappointed I didn\'92t get to see the drones in action. Richard seemed to know everything was fine and really enjoyed the show. But what about the repercussions, quite a few of your colleagues died here today. There will be calls for payback.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Anyone dumb enough to try to a direct assault on the Shakti mansion gets what they deserve. Such a lack of respect for the rest and repose of the upper executive class.\'94 Hayley was just busting to tell Sarah the news and managed to bring the conversation around. \'93I would not worry too much about police retaliation, after all, you are speaking to Commissioner Lanning.\'94 Hayley winced as Sarah screamed with delight.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Congratulations! It worked out pretty much as you hoped.\'94 Sarah was thrilled. \'93Your competition is out of the picture?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Yes and he\'92s is in big trouble for the raid.\'94 Hayley laughed.Victory felt good. \'93We have to meet tonight. I am in the mood for a celebration.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Okay. That\'92s if I can get Grandma to hand over my son.\'94
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 - - - 
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Holy Aunt Hayley, the most powerful law officer in the land, made sure her wig was on straight and she was obscured from security vid as she made her way to The Quarter. Any electronic contraption that could trace her location was cast aside and left in her office. She was never dumb enough to get cyber-implant, so there had been no need for home neurosurgery.
\f0 \

\f2 The Elvi had spent most of their working lives in hospitality and arranging an extravaganza at a moment\'92s notice presented few obstacles. There was only one place the all of the Elvi could congregate at once, the old sports stadium. The upgrades since Kleo\'92s funeral had been progressing steadily. The bathroom facilities were second to none and it was considered an honour to jag the position of bathroom attendant. 
\f0 \

\f2 As Hayley made her way inside the vast stadium, towards the executive boxes, she side-stepped her way through small bands of Elvis cleaners scuttling about polishing the floors and windows, all the while belting out tune after tune in perfect harmony. Elvis Security had been tight, but they had been smart enough to get the Dawks on board for some of the catering and at each entrance couple of Dawks would hand everyone a complimentary bottle of water reminding the Elvi, \'93Keep hydrated.\'94 Haley was was greeted at the door of the Royal Box by a very correct Elvis matre\'92d, 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We are honoured by your presence Holy Aunt Hayley. You are the last of the honoured guests to arrive. Follow me, honoured Aunt.\'94 He said, perfectly poised.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Thank you, but I would like to make my own way.\'94 Hayley said as politely as she could.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Of course. As my honoured guest wishes.\'94 Replied the matr\'92d, nose slightly bent out of place. \'93Make way, Holy Aunt coming through. She weaved her way through the crowd, to sighs of delighted recognition. 
\f0 \

\f2 The Blessed Mother, The Great Teacher and Holy Aunt Kathy were outside with the High Elvis, each holding a glass of wine, except for The Great Teacher who had a bottle of beer in each hand and one sticking out of his pants pocket. Chilo and Silo, dressed in their standard Druid attire, were standing to the side, speaking, no doubt, of things important as they leaned against the chunky handrail of a huge newly constructed deck. Jutting out into the stadium about 20 or 30 metres it could easily hold two hundred. Beyond the handrail and about 5 metres below was the playing field surface, quickly filling with Elvi. In the dimly lit stadium Holy Aunt Haley could see the ground was bright green and thick with precisely cut lawn. The effort that went in keeping the grass alive must have stupendous, she thought as she stared vacantly at the starless, pitch black sky. 
\f0 \

\f2 The stadium seating was almost full now, the buzz radiated outward and washed across Hayley like a warm, full body caress. She could see row after row of happy faces, enthusiastically engaged in chatter with their neighbour. Breathing in her success she turned to greet her friends.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Commissioner!\'94 The High Elvi called out, arms raised and waving about madly. Hayley strolled confidently to the group \'93Please join us. I have just heard of your promotion. Congratulations!\'94 They hugged and then Sarah, Cracker and Kathy joined in for a group hug.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Thank you, Thank you all.\'94 She beamed a white smile. \'93You can let go if you like, Cracker.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I am just so happy, Holy Aunt Commissioner.\'94 Cracker laughed as he disengaged.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Not funny.\'94 Smiling back at him. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93This is a very big night for the Elvi too.\'94 H.E.said. \'93We will finally be introducing Richard to his people. The plans have been gathering dust for months and now it is finally here. All thanks to you, Hayley\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We all had a role to play and you played yours perfectly your Highness.\'94 Hayley replied, keen to return the complement. \'93We may have one more act to play out tonight, I fear.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We are ready.\'94 The High Elivs whispered.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Waiter.\'94 Cracker called out to a passing Elvis. \'93Can we get another round\cf2 ? \cf0 Hayley what are we drinking tonight?\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Everything, I think, but I will start with champagne if there is any.\'94 Hayley was ready to cut loose.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You heard the lady\'94 Cracker said. \'93Champagne and keep them coming.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Yes, Great Teacher, the Holy Aunt\'92s glass will never be empty.\'94 The waiter backed away 4 paces and turned towards the bar. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I got a spare beer, if you can\'92t wait.\'94 Cracker offered.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Please.\'94 She said and grabbed the neck of the bottle, poking out of Cracker\'92s pants pocket. \'93Still cold, excellent.\'94 She twisted the top and took a dainty sip before turning to Kathy. \'93I have not seen you for weeks. How are you?\'94 Hayley gazed upon Kathy\'92s slender arms and noted she was patch-less.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I\'92ve been busy, far too busy even, to organise a decent patching regimen.\'94 Kathy looked a bit glum. Sobriety clearly did not suit. \'93I spend most of the time arguing with Sarah\'92s friend Johnny. Everything is a battle with him and it never stops. He has a brilliant analytical mind, but he has not learned to share.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I am reconsidering the entire venture, but carry on until next week. Schedule a meeting and you can brief me, but for now we are here to have some fun.\'94 Hayley decided business was off the agenda. \'93Where are your patches? This is most unusual.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Don\'92t worry, I\'92m stocked up for a long night, but I wanted to ease into it for a change.\'94 Kathy, forced sober by \'91Johnny management duties\'92 had actually began to enjoy sobriety, in moderation. She tilted her glass toward her mouth and took small sip. \'93Mmm, not bad.\'94 The talk of patching cracked Kathy\'92s resolve and she nodded to Cracker who slipped his hand into his jacket pocket, stood to her side and imperceptibly slipped a patch in to her palm. Unceremoniously and for anyone to see, she slapped the random patch on the inside of her thigh, just above the hem-line. She had no idea whether it was an upper of a downer or a combo, but she was keen to find out. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Here\'92s to us!\'94 Sarah raised her glass and let out the standard \'93Wooooo!\'94 Thus announcing to the crowd there is a bunch of girls here and they are drinking champagne.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Wooo!\'94 said Hayley, Kathy, Sarah in synchronised cheer and \'91clinked\'92 glasses high, hugged, giggled and drained their glasses. Holding them, again high, they hailed down a waiter. \'93Wooo! Ha, Ha, Ha!\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Where is Richard?\'94 Hayley asked Sarah.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93In the security area, downstairs. They will bring him up when then time comes.\'94 Sarah took a swig of her champagne flute. \'93My security team now have state of the art PPP\'92s. Eloise decided to give them an upgrade.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Give?\'94 Hayley would have believed \'91sold\'92, but \'91give\'92? 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93She wanted overwhelming firepower protecting my boy.\'94 They clinked glasses and drank a silent toast. \'93Do you think he is actually safe now\cf2 ? \cf0 We still have that problem\'94 Sarah pointed to the bar area. Agent Jones had made his entrance, dressed in his hooded cape and \'91grass\'92 crown. The crowd became silent very quickly, even the band stopped playing.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Oh, dear.\'94 Hayley said as her hand covered her mouth.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We had hoped he would have been taken care of by now.\'94 Said the High Elvis. \'93It looks like it will happen here.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We have that covered don\'92t we?\'94 Sarah asked, suddenly fearing for Richard. \'93Perhaps I will check in on Richard.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We have it covered.\'94 The High Elvis assured her. \'93Great Saviour! Most revered one.\'94 He called out across the length of the deck. The Elvis-elite remained silent but parted, allowing free passage directly to the the High Elvis. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I am well my leader, born again, as it were.\'94 Agent Jones was sickeningly cheerful.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Come and enjoy the hospitality of ALL YOUR ELVIS BROTHERS AND SISTERS.\'94 H.E. said to the entire mob. The Elvi returned to their conversations and the band burst back into life. 
\f0 \
