\f2 \cf0 - - -
\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Haloren Smythe only took one gun on his suicide mission. Intel-chatter indicated major Elvi activity at the stadium which meant it was very likely Agent Jones, The Great Saviour of the Elvi, would be there. He had no real plan, but he knew if he could be close he would succeed. Getting away alive was not an option. He had no life now anyway. All bridges burnt and all debts called in. 
\f0 \

\f2 Approaching the stadium the fabulous sounds of the Elvis concert belting out became louder and louder. He followed the din to a fence erected around a condemned section of the stadium. He gained entry through one of the old rickety grandstands and before skulking from shadow to shadow, he was within striking distance of the main party deck. All security in his path, mysteriously absent at every turn. Even with no discernible opposition it took an eternity navigate through a maze of corridors and walkways but he was now on final approach. He resolved to move quickly and with purpose, making no further attempt at hiding and hoped luck would be with him. He slowed to a confident stroll as he approached the maitre\'92d (?). 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Good evening, I am\'85\'94 but he was cut off.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You would be the assassin. We have been expecting you.\'94 The maitr\'92d said bluntly to a stunned killer. \'93This way, sir.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 He entered the front bar area and was met no resistance. Apart from a few sideways glances, the elites gathered there barely seemed to notice him until he had made his way into the centre of the vast deck. For the second time that night, the gathering slowly parted causing a straight path to the High Elvis and his party of honoured guests.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93You are earlier than expected, assassin, but we are ready.\'94 The High Elvis challenged the lone gunman.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I am here for Agent Jones.\'94 Haloren stuttered. \'93Stand aside.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Okay.\'94 The High Elvis and his friends stood aside, leaving the Great Saviour a lone figure.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What is going on your highness?\'94 Agent Jones was confused.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Standing before you, my Elvi.\'94 The High Elvis, now broadcasting over the PA, drew a deep long breath. \'93\'85is Agent Jones, a most dishonourable man. He tortured his own team of Elvi to ingratiate himself with the enemy. He bit their ears off!! We all saw the bodies of our brave brothers.\'94 A massive collective sigh of shock and disgust arose from the crowd below.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93I did nothing of the sort.\'94 Denial was all he had.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Holy Aunt Hayley.\'94 The High Elvis took a step back.
\f0 \

\f2 Hayley was momentarily mute, not expecting to make this speech in front of her rival, Haloren Smythe. She knew he was dead no matter what he did, so he may as well accept this one last mission. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Thank you High Elvis. The bite marks on the ears of the victims exactly matches the bite pattern of Agent Jones. His DNA was found in the wounds. Furthermore, he tortured and attempted to kill the Great Teacher with a weapon that was identified in the murder of a mother and two children. Children he killed just to cover his own incompetence. Proved by ballistics. It is also rumoured he tortured and killed two surveillance operatives, again in an attempt to cover his own incompetence. He is untrustworthy and will turn on you all as soon as it is convenient. This is a sanctioned termination of a contract and there is no reason to interfere.\'94 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Oh, come on! You were in on all this?\'94 Haloren stupidly blurted out. \'93That video was all bullshit?\'94 
\f3\i I was right, I was fucking right.
\f2\i0  He could get word to the CEO but he knew it would do no good. He now realised the magnitude of his defeat. She had crushed him.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Silence! No one owes you any explanations. This man, this assassin, was behind the plot to kill the One-after-the-One!\'94 She took two steps back again exposing Agent Jones to his fate. \'93You are here for a reason, get on with it and then do the right thing.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 Each Elvi took out a gleaming PPP and watched carefully as Haloren raised his pistol and walked toward his target first slowly before breaking into a trot. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93No, No. I can tell you about the discs. I can tell you all of their plans. Please.\'94 Agent Jones managed to blurt out before his head exploded. Doing the right thing, Haloren wedged the gun under his chin and pulled the trigger.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Clean up this mess\'94 The High Elvis called out. \'93Now the real party can begin.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 The Elvi erupted into cheer and all began to sing a the Elvis classic \'91Unlucky Brain\'92. First recorded a few months earlier, as a parody of Alexander Shakti, they had changed the lyrics for this special occasion and gave a short rendition.
\f0 \
