\f2 \cf0 As they sang, Sarah and Cracker looked at each other and began to laugh. Both were splattered in Agent-brains and picked chunks from one another\'92s face and hair. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93What was that slogan again?\'94 Cracker said directly into Sarah\'92s ear.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Brains, but no stains!\'94 They laughed in unison, recalling their very first encounter. \'93We all need to get cleaned up.\'94
\f0 \

\f2 The others in their elite group had not faired any better and were each wiping their faces with handkerchiefs, serviettes and anything else they could lay their hands on. Holy Aunt Kathy shook her head of dark hair, dislodging a couple of bone fragments and a few bloody teeth which bounced and lightly clattered on the deck. 
\f0 \

\f2 A wave of Elvis cleaners appeared out of the crowd and set to whisking away the bodies, mopping the deck and chasing down blood splatters. The Holy Aunts, Blessed Mother and The Great Teacher were spirited away to the private chambers of the High Elvis to take advantage of a quick shower and a set of new clothes. They returned to the party, resplendent in glittering dinner jackets and flared pants, to a resounding cheer from the Elvi, all similarly dressed.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93It\'92s time.\'94 The High Elvis couldn\'92t wait and turned to the interior of the stadium, now full and walked to the centre of the long handrail at the edge of the deck. He raised his hand high above his head. \'93My Elvis brothers and sisters! Welcome!\'94 A single ancient flood light, long thought extinct, burst into life, illuminating the highest ranking Elvis. \'93We have waited for this night for a very long time and now the waiting is over. We walk the path of science and reason, the way of the Dawkins!\'94 He paused as the deafening cheer slapped him in the face and dislodged his bouffant. \'93The one-after-the-one, made in the image of the Dawkins, is born to us and we are blessed with his presence tonight!\'94 Again the entire stadium erupted.
\f0 \

\f2 \'93We are honoured to have with us tonight, to help us celebrate this historic event, The Great Teacher, Holy Aunt Haley and Holy Aunt Kathy.\'94 Each was greeted with thundering cheers and applause as they were illuminated by a personal spot light, their jackets glimmering madly as they waved to the crowd, 100,000 strong. 
\f0 \

\f2 \'93Tonight we honour our dear departed Kleoboulos. We honour his wisdom and a his vision that this day would come. We honour the vision of his disciples, Chilo and Silo. This day we welcome our saviour, the one-after-the-one, King Richard I of the Elvi!\'94 It was fortunate that the massive stadium did not also include a roof, as it would have been launched into orbit, such was the cacophony of joy that erupted. The band kicked-in in a effort to drown out the crowd and after a lengthy battle the band seemed to win out, finally allowing the High Elvis to continue. 
\f0 \

\f2 A glass bounded commentary box, high above in the old media centre, exploded into angelic light as the band again kicked into high gear, belting out the tune of a yet to be released song of praise. The High Elvis himself stepped forward and pointing directly above, the crowd saw the Holy Mother standing behind the glass holding Richard high above her head for all to see. For a moment there was absolute silence. The king looked down from on high and raised a pudgy little hand and waved regally to the adoring throngs. It was both the cutest thing any had seen and the most spiritually uplifting experience of their lives, forever binding them as one. All at once the Elvi on the playing field fell to their knees and held there hands aloft, staring upward with adoring eyes. Just as quickly and in time with the music they all stood up, arms still raised, shaking their hands wilding they now began to scream to the sky, \'93He has come, he has come\'85\'94
\f0 \

\f2 \'93It\'92s looking up people, it\'92s looking up.\'94 The High Elvis, without breaking eye contact with Richard began to sing. No Elvis standing before him had ever heard this song, but they knew implicitly the correct dance moves, pulling off some impressive instant choreography, raising the heads and hands high at the end of each verse.
\f0 \
